WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
Good morning, Hank. It's Sunday.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.380
so the Yeti and I are beginning this "gigantor" home renovation,

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:09.480
part of which is to replace these moldy basement walls with like non-moldy basement walls.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.840
And when the contractor came in to talk to us about it,

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:14.819
he was like: "Look, I recommend destroying the wall on your own.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.100
I mean it takes a professional to build a wall, but anybody can demolish a wall."

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.020
And now, Hank, a week later, I feel like I can say with authority and pride that

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:30.440
if anyone can demolish a wall, I can do something that no one can do: fail at demolishing a wall.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.800
And so, today, Hank, I'm going to share my unique talent with you.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.300
I am going to teach you how NOT to demolish a wall in six easy steps.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.160
Step one: the Octopus

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.540
So, Hank, my first strategy to try to tear down the wall --

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.700
this was pre-holes, by the way -- was to throw myself against it.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.680
I did this once before, actually, I threw myself against the wall to find out if I was an octopus

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.800
because, you know, octopi stick to walls but people don't.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.379
And when I did it that first time I felt the wall shake a little, so the first thing I tried was the octopus.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.040
[sound of John hitting the wall] [John groans]

00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:10.049
Gah

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.760
Still not an octopus.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:19.760
So that didn't work. Then I moved on to step two: calling former Soviet Leader Mikhail Gorbachev.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.180
"Oh, hi Mr. Gorbachev? Tear down that wall!"

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:26.640
And he was like, "Shto? Shto? Ya ne govario po anglisky. (What? What? I do not speak English.)"

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.020
You know, and then, of course I remember he doesn't speak English, and plus he lives in Russia,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.060
so it'd be like totally expensive to find Indiana just to tear down my basement wall...

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.080
and so I moved on to step 3: calling Dad.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.220
Dad said I needed a crowbar, but I felt like crowbars are like handguns, you know?

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.620
I understand that I have a constitutional right to own a crowbar,

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.079
but I don't really feel like I need one unless I'm a career criminal.

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:53.849
But he eventually convinced me to go out and buy a crowbar, whereupon, I commenced with step four:

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.460
attempting to use a crowbar.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.240
[sounds of the crowbar against the wall]

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.300
[John letting out sounds of frustration]

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.760
Which went like that for about an hour and a half. Then, I moved on to step 5:

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:10.640
getting really angry, which is where the holes in the wall that you see come into play.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:15.720
Basically, Hank, I got really mad and I started to hit the wall, which I don't mean metaphorically.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.280
[yelling out of frustration]

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.440
HULK SMASH

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.289
Then I did that until I felt sleepy, whereupon, I took a nap.

00:02:25.289 --> 00:02:27.620
And then, when I woke up I moved on to step six,

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.240
which if you're going to NOT demolish a wall you'll want to save until the very end of your experience.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.740
Step six is checking to make sure

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.620
there is no active electrical wiring in the places where you are willy-nilly throwing your steel crowbar.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.460
Which as it turns out, there is.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:46.439
So that's how you DON'T demolish a wall. You do the Octopus, you call Mikhail Gorbachev,

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:51.119
you call your dad, you get a crowbar, you go bonkers, you take a nap, you wake up from the nap

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:56.920
check for electrical wiring, and then declare yourself a proud and epic fail.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.660
Oh home renovation, you have begun so auspiciously.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.440
Hank, you'll see me on Tuesday

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.860
But will you see the wall? Only time will tell.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.560
So, Hank, I think when you get a crowbar,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.300
you're supposed to want to like smash stuff with it, but that wasn't my initial reaction.

00:03:12.301 --> 00:03:16.309
My first reaction was that I wanted to treat it as a cane and kind of do a dance?

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:19.369
Like... do do do do do do do do

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.789
Do do do do do do do do do do do!

